===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a [[mighty]] manner; with strength or force.
# Enormously, to a great extent.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=1960-09|author=G. Freeman Allen|title=I.C.I. fertiliser goes by rail from Tees-side|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=533|text=The Billingham fertiliser traffic has grown '''mightily''' in the past few seasons.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Bill Mears|title=Supreme Court: Old habits die hard|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2014/07/01/politics/scotus-analysis/index.html|date=2014-07-01|passage=The Supreme Court tried '''mightily''' to come together.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Dawn Szymanski & Chandra Feltman|title=The psychological toll of being a Hooters waitress|magazine=w:Business Insider|url=https://www.businessinsider.com/the-toll-of-being-a-hooters-waitress-2015-8|date=2015-08-31|passage=While casual-dining chains like Applebee’s and Olive Garden are struggling '''mightily''', many breastaurant chains reported 30% or more growth in the last few years.}}
# {{lb|en|US|regional}} Thoroughly; entirely.
#: {{ux|en|He sounded '''mightily''' proud of himself.}}

